We've been getting a lot more posts about how hard 3.0 is.  When I installed
the game, I installed the -DHARD version--2.3 having become boring and too
easy.  Initially, I got killed a lot and was getting fed up.  However, after
playing some more and reading the spoilers I'm getting much more successful
(no where near winning, but consistently down to at least level 8 - 10, 
sometimes 15 - 20).  I think the game is balanced about right.  Anyway, the
reason for this post was to get some idea of the proportion of people playing
the HARD version.  I would guess most people are--is this right.

Run-time levels of difficulty seem like a good idea.  I guess this would need
a high score table and a set of bones files for each level of difficulty--you
can't have a player on a hard level inheriting the goodies from an easy game.
